    "contentHash": "00f6a10abddd15d67225de4eca3a0d2e36a97043ef9e90c8b9f7911af88b0372",
    "notes": {
      "item": "0046's ruling on return as built: a policy toward a protected population, never acting on people as a quantity. Return is watched, floored at approve_holding (0074, G-1.5c), expires with the confiscation act (B10) and is labelled plainly (Q6). Its basis is the 1850 law and the claimant's demand, true on 27 May, with no invented advocate. approve_holding is Cameron's, in a state-neutral paraphrase of his terms (C1, Q4). The text names the commander from State, never assuming Butler. Inaction is a floored policy (G-1.5g). Whoever carries the order answers by his own practice. No staff line recommends return."
    }
  }
